Claim: phi_n^{(n-1)} = phi_n^{(n)} = Q(n)/n EXACTLY (not up to O(1/n)).
Reason: at K=n-1 the single un-rerouted point x has f(x)=pi(x), and for a
uniform random permutation the MARGINAL of pi(x) is Uniform[n], independent
of the U_i.  So f is exactly a uniform random mapping.

